:: StoryTitle
Home


:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "B6F2FDE3-0D8B-4CC3-BAE6-HOME-CITY-LINK",
  "format": "SugarCube",
  "format-version": "2.37.3",
  "start": "Living Room",
  "zoom": 0.6
}


:: StoryInit
<<set setup.sharedVariables = ["visitedPark", "visitedObservatory", "visitedMuseum", "visitedBobaShop", "bookRead", "lastLocation"]>>
<<set setup.harvestUrlState = function () {
	var params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
	State.variables.visitedPark = params.get("visitedPark") === "1";
	State.variables.visitedObservatory = params.get("visitedObservatory") === "1";
	State.variables.visitedMuseum = params.get("visitedMuseum") === "1";
	State.variables.visitedBobaShop = params.get("visitedBobaShop") === "1";
	State.variables.bookRead = params.get("bookRead") === "1";
	State.variables.lastLocation = params.get("lastLocation") || "home";
}>>
<<set setup.storyUrl = function (target) {
	var params = new URLSearchParams();
	params.set("visitedPark", State.variables.visitedPark ? "1" : "0");
	params.set("visitedObservatory", State.variables.visitedObservatory ? "1" : "0");
	params.set("visitedMuseum", State.variables.visitedMuseum ? "1" : "0");
	params.set("visitedBobaShop", State.variables.visitedBobaShop ? "1" : "0");
	params.set("bookRead", State.variables.bookRead ? "1" : "0");
	params.set("lastLocation", State.variables.lastLocation || "home");
	return target + "?" + params.toString();
}>>
<<set setup.syncUrl = function () {
	window.history.replaceState(null, "", setup.storyUrl("home.html"));
}>>
<<run setup.harvestUrlState()>>
<<run setup.syncUrl()>>


:: Living Room {"position":"300,300","size":"100,100"}
The living room is warm and still. A yellow lamp leans over the sofa, and a slim book waits on the table as though it has been saving your place.

<<if $bookRead>>
The book is closed now. Its cover seems less yellow than you remember.
<<else>>
The book's cover is the color of old stage light.
<</if>>

* [[Read the book|The Book]]
* [[Go to the kitchen|Kitchen]]
* [[Go to the bedroom|Bedroom]]
* [[Go to the front door|Front Door]]


:: The Book {"position":"450,300","size":"100,100"}
<<set $bookRead = true>>
You open the book. The first page describes a city under a second moon, a museum full of masks, and a tower where observers chart the movement of impossible stars.

The words are calm. That makes them worse.

[[Close the book|Living Room]]


:: Kitchen {"position":"300,450","size":"100,100"}
The kitchen smells faintly of tea and rain. A cup sits beside the sink, empty except for a ring of amber at the bottom.

[[Return to the living room|Living Room]]


:: Bedroom {"position":"150,300","size":"100,100"}
The bed is neatly made. When you lie down, the rooms of the house soften around the edges, and the city comes back in pieces.

<<if !$visitedPark and !$visitedObservatory and !$visitedMuseum and !$visitedBobaShop>>
You have not brought the city home with you yet.
<<else>>
You remember:
<<if $visitedPark>>
* the park, with its paths crossing like old handwriting
<</if>>
<<if $visitedObservatory>>
* the observatory, where the sky felt close enough to bruise
<</if>>
<<if $visitedMuseum>>
* the museum, where every exhibit looked away first
<</if>>
<<if $visitedBobaShop>>
* the boba shop, bright and sweet against the rest of the day
<</if>>
<</if>>

[[Get up|Living Room]]


:: Front Door {"position":"300,150","size":"100,100"}
<<set $lastLocation = "frontDoor">>
<<run setup.syncUrl()>>
The front door is cool under your hand. Outside, the city waits with its lamps already lit.

<<link "Step into the city">><<run window.location.href = setup.storyUrl("city.html")>><</link>>

[[Return to the living room|Living Room]]
